# Chilli Intelligence Web -- environment configuration.
#
# Copy to .env and adjust, or set these as real environment variables /
# platform secrets. Nothing here is a secret by default -- the workbook is a
# business data file, not a credential -- but keep it out of version control
# if your copy contains data you don't want in git history.

# Full path to the master workbook. If unset, the app searches (in order):
#   1. this variable
#   2. ~/OneDrive/Desktop/Desktop/Shahaniya/AgriWatch/chilli dashboard/Chilli mastersheet for dashboard.xlsx
#   3. Chilli mastersheet for dashboard.xlsx in the project root
#   4. the same filename inside chilli_desktop/
# Leave unset to use the copy already committed at the project root.
# CHILLI_WORKBOOK=/app/Chilli mastersheet for dashboard.xlsx

# Host/port the production server (run_web_production.py) binds to.
# Most PaaS hosts (Render, Railway, ...) inject PORT automatically -- leave
# unset there. Set HOST=0.0.0.0 to accept connections from other machines
# when running locally (see README "Run on the network").
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=8060

# Optional: HTTP Basic Auth for the web app (see chilli_web/app.py). Set both
# to require a username/password before the dashboard renders. Leave unset
# to serve without authentication.
# CHILLI_WEB_USERNAME=
# CHILLI_WEB_PASSWORD=
